    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1775\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize Congregation Divrei Chaim of Monsey to file an\napplication for certain real property tax exemptions\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo authorize Congregation Divrei of Monsey to apply for a real\nproperty tax exemption for certain property in the Town of Ramapo,\ncounty of Rockland.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 authorizes the Town of Ramapo, county of Rockland, to accept\nfrom Congregation Divrei Chaim of Monsey an application for exemption\nfrom real property taxes.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCongregation Divrei Chaim is a school that purchased a property after\nthe deadline for the application for a religious exemption from the\nproperty taxes was due. As a non-for-profit organization if would be\nentitled to such an exemption if the organization had owned the\nproperty and filed an application for the exemption by the appropriate\ntaxable status date.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2015-16: S7952B - Rules\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATION :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
